---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href, name, repository } from '../lib/site';

const description =
  'What the localhost website and app collect: anonymous page views and download clicks on the site, two anonymous open events from the app, and how to turn them off.';
const url = (path: string) => new URL(path, Astro.site).toString();
const structuredData = [
  {
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'localhost privacy',
    description,
    url: url(href('privacy')),
    isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name, url: url('/') },
  },
];
---

<Base title="Privacy" {description} type="article" {structuredData}>
  <div class="container page">
    <header>
      <p class="plate-label">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="engraved">What localhost collects</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Very little, and nothing about your projects. Both the website and the app send anonymous usage events to
        <a href="https://posthog.com">PostHog</a>, so we can tell whether people who download localhost keep using it.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2 class="engraved">The app</h2>
      <div class="body">
        <p>
          When the app opens, it sends one event: <code>app_first_open</code> the first time, <code>app_opened</code> after
          that. Each carries only:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>a random id made on your computer the first time, not tied to you, your account or your machine;</li>
          <li>the app’s version, your operating system (macOS, Windows or Linux) and architecture;</li>
          <li>how it was installed: Homebrew, DMG, the Windows installer, <code>.deb</code>, <code>.rpm</code>, AppImage or a source build.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Never your projects, services, commands, paths, logs, environment variables, Secrets, host name or user name. No
          person profiles, no location lookup, no session recording. The <code>localhost</code> command and the MCP server
          send nothing.
        </p>
        <p>The app says this once, the first time it opens. It is on by default; to turn it off, any of these works:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Settings › General › <strong>Share anonymous usage data</strong>;</li>
          <li>set <code>DO_NOT_TRACK=1</code> in the environment the app starts with;</li>
          <li>set <code>LOCALHOST_TELEMETRY=0</code> (or <code>false</code>, <code>off</code>).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Development builds, test runs and builds in CI send nothing at all.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="engraved">The website</h2>
      <div class="body">
        <p>
          This site counts page views and a few named clicks, such as Download buttons, copied install commands and links
          to GitHub. It doesn’t record sessions or any other clicks. PostHog keeps an anonymous id in your browser’s storage
          to tell one visit from the next, and makes no person profile from it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="engraved">The rest</h2>
      <div class="body">
        <p>
          The site and the app use separate PostHog projects, and an id from one is never linked to the other. The tokens
          built into both can only send events, not read them. Nothing is sold or shared with anyone else.
        </p>
        <p>
          localhost is open source: the code that sends these events is
          <a href={`${repository}/blob/main/core/localhost-core/src/telemetry.rs`}>in the repository</a>, and the full list is
          in <a href={`${repository}/blob/main/docs/analytics.md`}>docs/analytics.md</a>. Questions go to
          <a href={`${repository}/issues`}>GitHub Issues</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    max-width: 960px;
    padding-top: 72px;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
  }
  header {
    margin-bottom: 56px;
  }
  h1 {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px);
  }
  .lede {
    margin-top: 20px;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .lede a,
  .body a {
    color: var(--accent-text);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 180px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 40px;
    padding: 40px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--separator);
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: clamp(24px, 2.4vw, 28px);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  .body {
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: 68ch;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .body p {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .body ul {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .body li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .body li::marker {
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }
  .body strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .body code {
    font-size: 0.88em;
    padding: 2px 5px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--fill);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .page {
      padding-top: 48px;
    }
    section {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 16px;
      padding: 32px 0;
    }
  }
</style>
